{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"20182e10078fae1ae6825fc20cb25bae420bbb7c8cf653c6ca33d4a1122ea0fa","slug":"index","location":"/intro.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Análisis Temporal y Demográfico de las Principales Causas de Muerte en Estados Unidos","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3","language":"python"},"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Valerie M","given":"Valerie","family":"M"},"name":"Valerie M","id":"contributors-Users\\luisc\\Myst\\myst-generated-uid-0"},{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Luis C","given":"Luis","family":"C"},"name":"Luis C","id":"contributors-Users\\luisc\\Myst\\myst-generated-uid-1"}],"github":"https://github.com/cantluis1/mortalidad-usa-analisis","keywords":["mortalidad","epidemiología","EE.UU.","análisis de datos"],"exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"intro.ipynb","url":"/intro-43c422951354c6137863bff4dea78617.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Valerie M y Luis C · 2025-05-06","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"IdJqA1q9lp"}],"key":"WL22iH54k6"}],"key":"YVqPUt3F2a"},{"type":"thematicBreak","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"i04HJV0JTE"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Introducción","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"z4VN1oNaxp"}],"identifier":"id-1-introducci-n","label":"1. Introducción","html_id":"id-1-introducci-n","implicit":true,"key":"xP87LGsxGy"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1.1. Contexto del Problema","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"cY7o0Zbj4M"}],"identifier":"id-1-1-contexto-del-problema","label":"1.1. Contexto del Problema","html_id":"id-1-1-contexto-del-problema","implicit":true,"key":"Io5Z42Akh4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Las enfermedades crónicas no transmisibles provocan la mayoría de los fallecimientos en Estados Unidos. El cáncer, enfermedades cardíacas, diabetes, enfermedades cerebrovasculares, Alzheimer, enfermedades respiratorias crónicas y enfermedades renales han sido motivos comunes de muerte. Además, existen causas externas (CDC/NCHS 2017). Se consideran factores externos de fallecimiento las lesiones no intencionales, los accidentes y el suicidio, conectadas con la manera en que vivimos y las circunstancias que nos envuelven.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"V8sNkl9V13"}],"key":"hUxIu2sDrG"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Como demostró James, Cossman, and Wolf (2018), que examinó 48 años de información sobre mortalidad entre 1968 y 2015, la mortalidad no es uniforme en todo el territorio, las disparidades geográficas son variables que se mantienen con el tiempo. En el sur rural, en los condados de Mississippi, Alabama, Kentucky y Tennessee, se localizan las zonas con más muertes. En la década de 1960, el número de muertes era alrededor de 50 por cada 100,000 habitantes; sin embargo, para el año 2015 ese número se incrementó a 220, los autores la llaman “The difference between the Heart of America and Dixiela”.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"Ex017W9urA"}],"key":"GSAq8U28Mk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Este estudio cubre el período 1999–2017 (Shah et al. 2019). Se demuestra la continuidad de las enfermedades crónicas como causa de muerte, así como la evolución de diferentes causas, como suicidios y accidentes, que cobran mayor importancia en las últimas décadas (Daugherty et al. 2019).","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"C6kEC4X9z7"}],"key":"LC8gGf3c2L"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1.2. Contexto del Dataset","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"BO08MBdofy"}],"identifier":"id-1-2-contexto-del-dataset","label":"1.2. Contexto del Dataset","html_id":"id-1-2-contexto-del-dataset","implicit":true,"key":"IOEHGXAzNt"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"El dataset utilizado es ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"LjXLi6nQSA"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“NCHS - Leading Causes of Death: United States”","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"S0haRnKqOE"}],"key":"rnV63rlE5g"},{"type":"text","value":". Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), la agencia nacional de salud pública de Estados Unidos. A través del National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) y National System of Vital Statistics (NVSS), los CDC recolectan todos los certificados de defunción emitidos en los 50 estados y el District of Columbia.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"xWou2IQr6f"}],"key":"JHl0v4tm0k"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":